+/*
+ * SM-T970 sensor DSP (SLPI): stage 1 of auto-brightness / auto-rotation (iOSPort work/sensors_scope/SCOPE.md).
+ * The light (VEML3328), motion (LSM6DSO) and compass (AK09918) chips hang off the SLPI sensor hub, not an APPS I2C bus,
+ * so the first step is to boot the SLPI and see which QRTR services it announces.
+ *
+ *   slpi        survey, reads only: SMEM items APPS<->SLPI, the SLPI's SMP2P state, PAS 12 support, whether the carveout
+ *               is XNU RAM, the firmware file and its program headers
+ *   slpi boot   once per boot: a kernel thread loads SL_FW through PAS 12 (init_image, mem_setup, segments,
+ *               auth_and_reset), waits for SMP2P ready, opens GLINK edge "dsps" channel IPCRTR, says QRTR HELLO and
+ *               records the NEW_SERVER packets (service 400 = the sensor client service)
+ *   slpi stat   the thread's progress and the services seen
+ *
+ * Polled, no interrupt: nothing here attaches IPCC SPI 229; the thread looks at SMP2P and the GLINK FIFO every 20 ms and
+ * rings the SLPI / AOP through the IPCC SEND register.
+ *
+ * Port of rui12366B/UniXNU-gts7xlwifi 88b34f9 package/T970Sensors.cpp levels 1-3 (BSD-2-Clause-Patent); the protocol
+ * code is that repository's QcomSmem/QcomSmp2p/QcomGlink/QcomQmp/QcomMdt/QcomRpmh/T970Ssc, copied unchanged into
+ * bsd/dev/qcom/. Addresses from the live T970 device tree (qcom,ssc@5c00000: pas-id 12, smem-id 424, pil_slpi_region
+ * 0x89200000 + 0x1500000 no-map, sensor_vdd = pm8150a_l8 1.8 V). Not tested on the device when written (z97).
+ */
+
